      "text": "saying is commonly reported among the Jews, Matt. 28:15. King of the Jews, Luke 23:38. Jews sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem, John 1:19. question between some of John’s disciples and the Jews, John 3:25. Jews have no dealings with the Samaritans, John 4:9. salvation is of the Jews, John 4:22. therefore did the Jews persecute Jesus, John 5:16. temple, whither the Jews always resort, John 18:20. dwelling at Jerusalem Jews, devout men, out of every nation, Acts 2:5. unlawful thing for a … Jew to keep company, Acts 10:28. preaching … to none but unto the Jews, Acts 11:19. assault … also of the Jews with their rulers, Acts 14:5. Jews which believed not, Acts 17:5. how many thousands of Jews there are which believe, Acts 21:20. I am … a Jew, born in Tarsus, Acts 22:3. to the Jew first, and also to the Greek, Rom. 1:16. Jew first, and also of the Gentile, Rom. 2:9. thou art called a Jew, and restest in the law, Rom. 2:17. he is not a Jew, which is one outwardly, Rom. 2:28. no difference between the Jew and the Greek, Rom. 10:12. preach Christ crucified, unto the Jews a stumblingblock, 1 Cor. 1:23. unto the Jews I became as a Jew, 1 Cor. 9:20. neither Jew nor Greek … ye are all one in Christ, Gal. 3:28 (Col. 3:11).",
